      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Instead of searching for the deep CMake script, you could add a Kconfig option that the board can enable.\n\u003e \n\u003e ```\n\u003e # Note - downstream symbol\n\u003e config ITE_ADDITIONAL_LTO_ALLOWLIST\n\u003e     depends on KERNEL_NO_LTO\n\u003e \n\u003e if(ITE_ADDITIONAL_LTO_ALLOWLIST)\n\u003e   function(kernel_lto_allow_list out_var)\n\u003e ```\n\nJust to confirm, is your suggestion that enabling a Kconfig option would directly activate the CMake function and use a fixed set of allow-listed .c files?\nIn our case, the additional LTO allowlist is specific to each board.\nFor example, DOMIKA needs timer.c, while another board may require a different set of files. Using a single boolean Kconfig option would effectively hard-code one allowlist for all boards, which doesn’t scale when their requirements differ.\n\n \n\u003e And I agree with Fabio\u0027s question - test if you can set `ADDITIONAL_ALLOWLIST` directly without the helper function.\n\nAs mentioned above in my response to Fabio.",
